<title>USA: U.S corp bond new issue drought may be shortlived.</title>
<headline>U.S corp bond new issue drought may be shortlived.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-08-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>The recent drought of new corporate debt issues may prove to be shortlived if the next batch of U.S. employment data takes on a bearish tone while market players head into end of quarter, dealers said.</p>
<p>&quot;We just have to see what happens next Friday with the employment numbers. That will set the tone,&quot; said one syndicate official.</p>
<p>He added, &quot;If it's (employment data) a weak number and the market rallies there will be a lot of new issues flowing in.&quot;</p>
</text>
